<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">MacMurrough dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Meic Murchada</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The MacMurroughs, in Irish Meic Murchada, were the leading family of the Uí Chennselaig and kings of Leinster from the 11th century, named after Murchad, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diarmait-mac-mael-na-mbo">Diarmait mac Máel na mBó</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diarmait-mac-murchada">Diarmait Mac Murchada</a> brought Anglo-Norman knights into Ireland in 1169. His descendants, the MacMurrough Kavanaghs, recovered power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wexford">Wexford</a> and Carlow, where Art MacMurrough Kavanagh defied Richard II, and they kept their independence until submitting to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-viii-of-england">Henry VIII</a>'s government.</p></div>
